{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwjeScNfWjVD9ddjWEpM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't confirmed the rule runs without errors: its status was still \"pending\" right after creation.\n\n**What the data holds:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` has web access logs with these fields:\n- `timestamp`\n- `response` (a string status code)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `url`\n\nThe only response codes present are 200 (12,832 requests), 404 (801) and 503 (441).\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-693aac7a Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Average bytes by extension\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-693aac7a-web-logs-overview-cb3eff1ac6fe.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-693aac7a 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]` over the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps are fixed, so the rule will only fire if 5xx requests are indexed with current timestamps. Its rule ID is `bc070da5-2ab7-44ec-9d9b-801275e7e718`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_read_input_tokens":20809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502},"output_tokens":485,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"ed7e69b0-7281-490c-adbe-be722d35fc1c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:46:46.588Z","request_id":"req_011CfwjeSPyN9wr1TqboUSZD"}
